message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "LivepatchDiff: Checking That Livepatch Builds Still Do What They Claim"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kazuru
    given-names: Seke
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-4099-1059"
    email: kazuruuni@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/kazuru-chidumbwe/livepatch-differential-harness"
url: "https://github.com/kazuru-chidumbwe/livepatch-differential-harness/tree/v0.2.2"
abstract: >-
  Differential test harness for Linux livepatch build pipelines. Combines ELF
  relocation triage, structural PLT32 bind checks, loadable mutants, PRE(A)
  revert-soundness gating, and per-case runtime predicates including hardened P3.
  Cite pin on Linux v6.6.47 plus Dirty Pipe PRE-gated packs on v5.16.10,
  second-pin smoke and depth on v6.1.119, six INCLUDE CVE contract packs, PRE(A)
  population scan, and Stanford minor-rev structural/timing suite.
keywords:
  - livepatch
  - Linux
  - differential testing
  - kpatch
  - ELF relocation
license: MIT
version: "0.2.2"
date-released: "2026-09-05"
